problems.problem:
Within the Milky Way, the Sun is located at the edge of the galactic disc, about 30,000 light-years from the centre (as shown in the figure, not to scale), around which it rotates with a speed of about 250 km/s. Determine:

1. how many years the Sun takes to complete one full revolution around the galactic centre (galactic revolution period);
2. the mass of the Milky Way under the hypothesis that the stars are distributed uniformly inside a sphere centred on the centre of the Galaxy;
3. the number of stars that make up the Galaxy, under the hypothesis that the mean mass of each of them is equal to that of the Sun.

