**The astronomer of Perugia**

An astronomer observes at 03:18:28 UT, from Perugia (latitude $= +43^\circ 07'$), a star which at its upper culmination has an altitude of $25^\circ 12'$. Knowing that at 00:00:00 UT the local sidereal time was $14^\mathrm{h}\,24^\mathrm{m}\,29^\mathrm{s}$:

